CHBingo
Copyright 2026 bateske

From CHBlackjack (https://github.com/bateske/CHBlackjack, Apache-2.0): the
input and frame pacing (now the CHGame library's chgame/Input.*), palette, drawing, outlined
lettering, effects, sound sequencer, flash saving, debug protocol, the PC
simulator and tools, the table's wall and rail, the caller (the dealer from
CHBlackjack's tables, with his expressions) and the broke screen's
lettering, adapted here by way of CHRoulette
(https://github.com/bateske/CHRoulette, Apache-2.0), whose screens,
presenter structure and redraw check this game started from. The "Bingo"
title lettering is drawn in the style of CHBlackjack's (Press Play On
Tape's) and CHRoulette's: its B is CHBlackjack's, its o CHRoulette's.

CHBlackjack is a derivative of "Blackjack" for the Arduboy by Press Play On
Tape - Simon Holmes (filmote), code, and Stephane C (vampirics), art
(https://github.com/Press-Play-On-Tape/Blackjack, Apache-2.0). The caller
is Press Play On Tape's dealer, recoloured and retouched by hand; the "YOU
ARE BROKE" lettering and the 3x5 pixel font in the CHGame library
(platform/board/arduino/CHGame/libraries/CHGame/src/chgame/Draw.cpp) are Press Play On Tape's.

From CHChess (https://github.com/bateske/CHChess, Apache-2.0): the pointing
glove, the soft clock ticks and the shake routine.

Everything else - the rules, the hall, the cards and their carousel, the
power-ups, the jackpot and the presentation - is
new, under the Apache License 2.0 (LICENSE).
